From 3b40202f9d772f43b061556e4335be1e0a827cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Heaton <rob@northwestlinux.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:42:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] USB3: report SuperSpeed in the root hub GET_STATUS speed
 decode

Map xHCI port speed ID 4 (SuperSpeed) to UPS_SUPER_SPEED. Until a
SuperSpeed port is exposed through the emulated root hub this never
triggers; it is groundwork.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 c/xhci | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/c/xhci b/c/xhci
index 0061097..446571a 100644
--- a/c/xhci
+++ b/c/xhci
@@ -3135,6 +3135,9 @@ xhci_root_ctrl_start(usbd_xfer_handle xfer)
 		case 3:
 			i = UPS_HIGH_SPEED;
 			break;
+		case 4:
+			i = UPS_SUPER_SPEED;
+			break;
 		default:
 			i = 0;
 			break;
